  SimpleStack
    Header 2|Repeater
    Text Layouts can iterate over a dataset.
    PreText
      Text:
        Data:Purchases
          Text:
            [off][{"ID":3, "Item":"Rabbit Food", "Amount":29.99, "VendorID":3}
            ,{"ID":1, "Item":"Candy", "Amount":1.50, "VendorID":1}
            ,{"ID":2, "Item":"Toilet Seat", "Amount":99.99, "VendorID":2}
            ,{"ID":4, "Item":"Light Bulbs", "Amount":9.49, "VendorID":1}
            ,{"ID":5, "Item":"Sink", "Amount":75.00, "VendorID":2}]

    Text Every layout control supports a repeat function. Here we do the most basic iteration, but it can be used to create grids, lists, or anything your imagination desires.
    Header 3|SimpleStack
    PreText
      Text:
        [off]SimpleStack
          DataSource: Purchases
          Header 3|=*.Item
          Text ID: [=*.ID] Cost: [=*.Amount]
    Text To use, simply assign a dataset property and create child controls as normal. For binding, specify * instead dataset name. =*.fieldname
    Text The * signifies the current row to bind to in the iterator. Bindings remain 2 way, and if bound to an editable control, changes will automatically be applied back to the dataset.
    Text There are also code callbacks for tax and Product Number.
    SimpleStack:RepeatStack
      DataSource: Purchases
      Header 4|=*.Item
      Text ID: [=*.ID] Cost: [=*.Amount]
      Text With 6% Tax:
      Text Product Number: 
    gap

    Header 3|List
    Button:AddVendorButton Add
    List
      DataSource: Vendors
      Text =*.Name